    heapq.heapify(ready)
    order = []
    while ready:
        n = heapq.heappop(ready)
        order.append(n)
        for d in dependents[n]:
            waiting[d].discard(n)
            if not waiting[d]:
                heapq.heappush(ready, d)
    if len(order) != len(nodes):
        raise ValueError("dependency cycle")
    return order
```

Kahn's algorithm: start with nodes that have no prerequisites, release dependents as their prerequisites finish. If some nodes never become ready, there's a cycle. Good tests shouldn't depend on each other, but setup pipelines, migration steps and build graphs do.

